# HARD STOP: no servers, no CDP, no mock testing

The human runs the apps. The agent only edits code.

## Never start servers

Do not start, restart, background, or kill the main processes from the terminal:

- APIs: `go run ./cmd/server`, `bun run dev:api`, anything listening on 8080–8082
- Admin, frontend, theme: `bun run dev`, `next dev`, `next start`

Do not `kill` listeners to “replace” a server. If a server is down, say so and stop. Do not wait on health checks or poll `/v1/*` as a substitute for running the app.

## Never CDP or browser automation

Do not use browser tools, Chrome DevTools Protocol, snapshots, screenshots, lock/unlock, or click/type/fill in a page to verify work.

## Never mock-up testing

Do not drive the UI as a fake user. Do not open localhost in a browser, walk through drawers, or “verify” layouts and autofill in a session. Unit tests of code you changed are fine. Shipping the code is enough.
